  "title": "Speaking So Children Feel Safe",
  "content": "Communication is more than the words we use—it is the tone, body language, and emotional presence behind those words. Children are highly sensitive to how adults speak to them. A calm, warm tone helps children feel safe and respected, while harsh or unpredictable communication can create fear or defensiveness.\n\nThis lesson explores how parents can use communication to build trust rather than control. When parents speak with clarity, kindness, and consistency, children are more likely to listen and cooperate. Positive communication does not mean avoiding boundaries; it means expressing them in ways that support connection.\n\nParents learn how to shift from reactive communication to intentional communication, creating a home environment where children feel heard and valued.",
